## Secrets

`.env` holds an agentic request-signing secret that was generated for you — never something you
choose or pass in — plus, if you generated this bundle with `--storage s3`, your bucket
credentials. It is readable by its owner only; keep it out of version control and treat it as a
credential store. Regenerating keeps the secret; pass `--rotate-secrets` to replace it, then
restart the whole stack.

## Storage

This bundle was generated with `--storage ${storage}`. Bucket credentials and per-job LLM
provider keys are stored in plaintext under that backend — restrict access to it the same way
you would any other credential store.

## Stopping it

```
docker compose down
```

Add `-v` to also remove the named volumes (database, SonarQube data, storage, signing
material) — this is destructive and cannot be undone.
